            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was delicious! Very cool and refreshing! I made the six servings (not realizing how much it would make) and drank it all (which is alot for a thirteen year old)! It was a nice change from the usual mango lassi I make."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Alexandra Lynch"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a really good basic recipe. I followed another reviewer in substituting milk for the water, and added a half cup of pureed pineapple and two tablespoons of lime juice, and then sweetened with Splenda to taste, along with a shake of cardamom. Sweet-sour pineapplelime deliciousness we'll definitely do again.",
            "datePublished": "2016-09-22T01:09:38.203Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MariaV"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This tasted nothing like the lassi's I've had at Indian restaurants. It is very sour, there isn't a hint of sweetness with only 2tsp of sugar. Adding 4 TBS of sugar made it sweet, but it still didn't have the flavor of a lassi. It needs rosewater and perhaps something else. I hope I can find a better recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2011-05-01T15:54:02.480Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GRANOLACOWGIRL"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I followed the recipe for my hubby and I, but added some frozen blueberries at the end. Delish!!\n\nThen, I customized it for our child by adding a dallop of natural honey to make it sweeter. The result was a healthy version of the \"Yop\" drink that kids like. All the taste but none of the fructose glucose!",
            "datePublished": "2011-02-06T18:17:33.163Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Fairy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Too watery. It's way better with ice-cold milk than water. Water is used only by Indian restaurants for profit. Real lassi is all milk and yogurt, no water.",
            "datePublished": "2011-05-10T09:57:56.060Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cupcake Princess"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used a tablespoon of sugar, added a 1/2 teaspoon of rose water, and didn't add the salt. I used about a 1/2 cup of water and the consistency was perfect. Thanks for the great recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2011-01-21T14:51:54.753Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Benjamin Garn Booth"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The only reason I'm giving this 4 stars instead of 5 is because I had to add 8 teaspoons instead of just 2 to make this taste like authentic Indian lassi that I've had. If you add about that much sugar, it is just like the real thing!",
            "datePublished": "2009-08-15T11:35:33.437Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Katrina"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I would not recommend using non fat yogurt! I had to add something to make it taste sweeter and went with chocolate syrup for the flavor and then it was okay. Next time I will stick to regular yogurt.",
            "datePublished": "2011-06-16T13:59:28.897Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JOSIE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I turned this drink into a fruit lassi by adding some banana and mango. I used about 2 cups of yogurt. I also used 1/2 milk and 1/2 water and added some cardamom and rose water to give a little more flaovr.",
            "datePublished": "2004-09-09T06:21:09.450Z"
          },
          {
